na Tomashova"] " (RUS). Britain’s Kelly Holmes had won a bronze in this event in 1994, but had not done much since then. However, earlier in Athina she had won a surprising gold medal in the 800. The final was run at a quick pace, led out by Russia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/109515"} "Nataliya Yevdokimova"] ". Holmes bided her time, running in the pack thru the final curve.  She pulled into the lead at the start of the final straight, and nobody could catch her as she completed the 800/1,500 double. Tomashova closed quickly to get the silver medal. In third place " [:a {:href "/athletes/104950"} "Maria Cioncan"] " (ROM) surprised with a PR of 3:58.39 to get the bronze medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1809"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/68679"} "Kelly Holmes"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "4:05.58 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "4:04.77 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "3:57.90 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2949"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/88925"} "Tatyana Tomashova"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RUS.png"}] "RUS"]] [:td {} "4:06.06 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "4:06.80 (3 h1)"] [:td {} "3:58.12 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2780"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/104950"} "Maria Cioncan"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROU"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middl